## Web UI

- **Full port target:** User-facing features must eventually live in the Web shell + bridge — see [docs/WEBVIEW_HYBRID_POLICY.md](docs/WEBVIEW_HYBRID_POLICY.md). Do not treat classic JUCE-only panels as permanent.

## Engineering constraints

- Broader **engine / services / nodes / scripting** paths benefit from careful stability review; prefer repro + tests for crash fixes.
- Prefer a dedicated dev build tree: **`build-merged`** (see VS Code tasks and [`.claude/skills/element-build-and-package/SKILL.md`](.claude/skills/element-build-and-package/SKILL.md)). If your machine cannot write there (e.g. permissions), use **`build-bugfix`** or another writable dir and point `compile_commands.json` / tasks to match.
- Avoid assuming **`build/`** is fresh; it may be a stale CMake tree from another path.
- **Never use `using namespace juce;` in headers** — use `juce::` (allowed in `.cpp` only per project convention).
- **New `.cpp` files**: CMake uses `file(GLOB_RECURSE)` — reconfigure after adding sources.

